KZ3 patch 1155 (SPU pass 145, diagnostic, needs KZ3_WAITSTAT=1): splits every untimed sys_event_queue_receive into the REAL WAIT (sleep start -> the
sender's push stamp q->ws_wake: the sender was late) and the WAKE LATENCY (push stamp -> the receiver runs again: the host's wake path), per queue id and
guest lr of the receive wrapper. "[evq-lat] q=N lr=0xL calls=.. slept=.. wait_us mean/p50/p90=.. lat_us mean/p50/p90=.." every 10 s on stderr.
Walker-plan step 8c: pass 131 measured 0.22 ms per receive x ~300/s on ppu-main (frametrace of spu130-a2: 5343 receives in 20 s, median 102 us, p90 668 us,
max 2.8 ms: a spread far wider than one wake path, so mostly sender lateness; this table settles it per queue). Off (default) = no clock reads,
no prints. Helper header runtime/platform/kz3_evq_lat.h; host test tools/spu/test_evq_lat.sh.

